{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{
  "coverage": [
    {"reason":"Interpreted through competing accountability and substantive-performance readings of paragraph 10; neither makes outsourcing a release from responsibility.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0"},
    {"reason":"Footnote 1 reinforces full responsibility, permits outsourced performance, and makes the Appendix reference conditional on applicability.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224"},
    {"reason":"Provides a distinct substantive requirement for proper ownership records and operational compatibility, relevant to evaluating fulfillment beyond retained authority.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729"},
    {"reason":"Interpreted with footnote 5 through competing readings of the demonstration trigger; confirmation is unqualified in the main text.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944"},
    {"reason":"Supplies minimum assurance content and a confidence standard, but its unqualified demonstration language creates tension with paragraph 14's request condition.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185"},
    {"reason":"Paragraph 15 separately conditions obtaining third-party audit or verification on an SFC request; paragraph 14 does not itself prescribe that evidential method.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u5.1464"},
    {"reason":"Paragraph 16 separately conditions obtaining a satisfactory legal opinion supporting the application on an SFC request.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u6.1694"},
    {"reason":"The register duty identifies the scheme, trustee or appointed person as operational actors. Its repetition in the next unit does not create an additional duty.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u7.1802"},
    {"reason":"The complete 6.8 excerpt separates ongoing register maintenance from advising the Commission of register locations on request; footnote 1 preserves Product Provider responsibility despite such arrangements.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u8.1941"},
    {"reason":"Valuation-specific supervision language illustrates an express conduct standard, but cannot automatically supply the tokenisation standard or extend its management-company scope.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u9.2169"},
    {"reason":"Parallel retained responsibility applies to intermediaries issuing or substantially involved in issuance of securities they intend to deal in or advise on. Applicability requires those separate actor and activity facts.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u10.2702"},
    {"reason":"Intermediary due diligence and pre-activity satisfaction with controls are separate obligations; their actors, activities and Appendix dependencies cannot be silently imported into Product Provider requirements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045"}
  ],
  "dimensions": [
    {"dimension":"scope","explanation":"The principal actor is the Product Provider. Operational register actors under 6.8, valuation management companies under 6.11C, and intermediaries under paragraphs 13 and 17–18 have distinct scopes. Overlap requires actual role and activity facts.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u7.1802","dc689bdf0ffcf.u8.1941","dc689bdf0ffcf.u9.2169","dc689bdf0ffcf.u10.2702","dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045"],"status":"PROPOSED"},
    {"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"The packet does not operationally define ultimate responsibility, soundness, proper records, integrity, SFC satisfaction or high confidence. Allocation of authority, supervisory conduct and achieved outcomes are different evidence categories; none is defined as an independently sufficient test.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729","dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},
    {"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"Outsourcing expressly does not remove Product Provider responsibility. Applicability qualifies the reference to Appendix factors. The SFC request condition qualifies demonstration in paragraph 14 and obtaining evidence in paragraphs 15–16, although footnote 5's unqualified wording supports a competing demonstration reading.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0ffcf.u5.1464","dc689bdf0ffcf.u6.1694"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},
    {"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The Product Provider provisions use should; 6.8 uses must, and 6.11C combines shall for care in selection, appointment and monitoring with should for supervision and review. The packet does not establish their wider legal enforceability. Confirmation, demonstration, third-party verification and legal opinion remain distinct acts.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0ffcf.u5.1464","dc689bdf0ffcf.u6.1694","dc689bdf0ffcf.u8.1941","dc689bdf0ffcf.u9.2169"],"status":"PROPOSED"},
    {"dimension":"time","explanation":"Responsibility continues despite outsourcing. Paragraph 14 distinguishes unqualified confirmation from requested demonstration on its main-text reading; paragraphs 15–16 require relevant requests. No calendar deadline or confirmation frequency is supplied. Intermediary paragraph 18 expressly requires satisfaction before related activities; valuation supervision is ongoing with periodic review.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0ffcf.u5.1464","dc689bdf0ffcf.u6.1694","dc689bdf0ffcf.u9.2169","dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},
    {"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Footnotes 1 and 5 must be read with their parent provisions. Footnote 5 depends on all of paragraphs 10–13, which are not fully supplied. Footnote 2 and the referenced Appendix Parts A and B are absent. The supplied intermediary paragraph 13 is not a substitute for paragraph 13 in footnote 5's own document.","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185","dc689bdf0ffcf.u10.2702","dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What applicable standard determines when retained responsibility under paragraph 10 has been discharged, and how does it distinguish authority, reasonable supervisory conduct and achieved soundness?",
    "What do the complete paragraphs 10–13, footnote 2 and applicable Appendix provisions require? Their absence prevents a complete assessment of footnote 5's minimum content.",
    "What actual governance powers, vendor arrangements, monitoring, remediation, operational tests and ownership-record evidence exist, and over what assessment period?",
    "Does footnote 5 merely elaborate paragraph 14's requested demonstration, or independently require an unsolicited demonstration to the SFC?",
    "Does SFC satisfaction govern demonstration alone or also confirmation, and does high confidence qualify only freedom from smart-contract vulnerabilities and security flaws or the whole minimum assurance?",
    "Has the SFC made a relevant request under paragraph 14, 15 or 16, and what subject, evidence, recipient and timing did it specify?",
    "Which entities also meet the separate scheme, trustee, management-company or intermediary scope conditions, and what confirmation timing and renewal practice applies?"
  ],
  "readings": [
    {
      "assumptions":["Paragraph 10 is read principally as allocating continuing accountability; separate substantive requirements retain independent force.","Governance powers and supervisory evidence are possible evidence of retained responsibility, not an enumerated safe harbour."],
