      "statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within Product Provider scope, true means that the request condition activating paragraph 14 demonstration is satisfied; false means it is not. Confirmation remains unqualified by that trigger. Both acts concern management and operational soundness, ownership record keeping and smart-contract integrity. Footnote 5 supplies minimum content: compliance with paragraphs 10–13 and assurance, with high confidence, of freedom from contract vulnerabilities or security flaws. The strongest grammatical reading attaches SFC satisfaction to demonstration and high confidence to the smart-contract assurance; broader attachment remains unresolved.",
